<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23620" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-ŏcŭlo</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum, 1, v. a.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
			inoculate</i>, i. e. <i>to ingraft an eye</i> or <i>bud of one tree into another</i> (post-Aug.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arbores ficorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					11, 2, 59</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>To implant</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">justitiae affectum pectoribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 1, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>To adorn</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bullis aureis inoculatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 6, p. 185, 21</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>